# Files that must never reach the web server.
#
# Vercel serves a static project by copying the repository into the
# deployment. Anything listed here is left out of that copy, so it cannot
# be fetched at any URL - it is not hidden, it is simply not there.
#
# This matters most on development branches. Vercel builds a preview
# deployment for every branch it sees, so without this file a push to a
# work-in-progress branch would put its unfinished pages and backend on a
# public https:// address.
#
# Nothing here is deleted from Git. All of it stays in the repository and
# in history; it is only excluded from what gets served.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 2A messaging backend - written, reviewed, NOT deployed.
#
# supabase/ holds the migrations and Edge Function source. staff/ is a
# sign-in page for an inbox that does not exist yet: publishing it would
# invite people to try credentials against a system with no backend, and
# would advertise the internal structure of one that is still being built.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
supabase/
staff/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal documentation.
#
# These are written for whoever maintains the site, not for customers.
# CHAT_BACKEND.md in particular describes the security model of the
# messaging system in detail - accurate, and not something to hand to a
# stranger unprompted.
#
# README.md is the same category: it explains how the site is built and
# maintained, and would otherwise be fetchable at /README.md. The bare
# name matches it at any depth, which also covers assets/img/README.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/
README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build and development tooling. Not part of the website.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
tools-bundle.js
node_modules/
.git/
.gitignore

# A GitHub Pages marker. It does nothing on Vercel, and it stays in the
# repository so the existing Pages build is unaffected - it is simply not
# part of the website.
.nojekyll

# Local secrets, if any ever exist on a developer's machine. They are
# gitignored too; this is the second lock on the same door.
.env
.env.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Camera originals for the gallery.
#
# The page serves only the .webp derivatives - nothing references these
# .jpg files. Left in, they were 21 MB of publicly fetchable downloads
# that no visitor ever asks for, still carrying the phone's make, model,
# firmware version and the exact minute each photo was taken. None of
# that belongs on a website.
#
# They stay in Git as the originals the derivatives are made from; they
# are simply not part of what gets served. The hero image lives at
# assets/img/work-enclosure.jpg, outside this folder, and is unaffected.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
assets/img/work/*.jpg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Firebase configuration and the Firestore rules tests.
#
# These are repository files, not website files. firestore.rules and
# firestore.indexes.json are deployed to Firebase by a deliberate,
# separate step - never by the web deploy - and publishing them would
# hand a stranger a precise map of the chat data model and of exactly
# which reads are permitted. tests/ is development tooling.
#
# Nothing here is needed to render a page.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
firestore.rules
firestore.indexes.json
firebase.json
.firebaserc
.firebase/
tests/
firebase-debug.log
firestore-debug.log
ui-debug.log

# This file itself. It names the paths it holds back, which is a map
# worth not handing out, and it is of no use to a browser.
.vercelignore
